===== README.md =====
     1	# Diedrico
     2	
     3	**An educational web application for teaching dihedral (orthographic) projection**
     4	
     5	Diedrico is an interactive learning tool designed to help engineering students understand and master dihedral projection—the fundamental technical drawing system used in engineering, architecture, and design. Unlike traditional CAD tools that focus on final results, Diedrico emphasizes the **constructive process**, making each geometric operation explicit and traceable.
     6	
     7	## 🎯 Purpose
     8	
     9	Diedrico is built for:
    10	
    11	- **Engineering students** learning orthographic/dihedral projection in technical drawing courses
    12	- **Instructors** who want to demonstrate construction sequences step-by-step
    13	- **Self-learners** exploring geometric principles of multi-view projection
    14	
    15	The application focuses on **how** drawings are constructed, not just what they look like. Every element has explicit dependencies, every construction is parametric, and geometric relationships update automatically when inputs change.
    16	
    17	## ✨ Key Features
    18	
    19	### Educational Focus
    20	- **Explicit construction process**: Every element is created through deliberate user operations
    21	- **Dependency tracking**: See how elements depend on each other through the Process Tree
    22	- **Parametric behavior**: Move points and watch dependent geometry update automatically
    23	- **No implicit entities**: All points, lines, and intersections must be created explicitly
    24	
    25	### Geometric Tools
    26	- **Multiple projection planes**: Work with horizontal (P_H) and vertical (P_V) planes simultaneously
    27	- **Rich element types**: Points, lines, segments, circles with multiple construction methods
    28	- **Specialized constructions**: Parallel/perpendicular lines, tangent lines, intersections
    29	- **Guide lines**: Create perpendicular guides for transporting distances between planes
    30	- **Distance transport**: Transfer measurements between projection planes using guides
    31	
    32	### Workspace
    33	- **2D primary view**: Main drawing area showing all projection planes in dihedral configuration
    34	- **3D auxiliary view**: Floating overlay for spatial understanding (read-only)
    35	- **Active plane system**: One plane receives new constructions; all planes remain visible
    36	- **Flexible navigation**: Pan (Shift + drag), zoom (mouse wheel), intuitive interactions
    37	
    38	### Modern Architecture
    39	- **Undo/Redo system**: Full command history with arbitrary undo depth
    40	- **Process Tree**: Visual representation of construction sequence and dependencies
    41	- **Google Drive integration**: Save and load projects from your Drive account
    42	- **Responsive UI**: Works on desktop browsers with clear visual feedback
    43	
    44	## 🚀 Getting Started
    45	
    46	### Prerequisites
    47	
    48	- **Node.js** 18.0.0 or higher
    49	- **npm** 9.0.0 or higher
    50	- Modern web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari)
    51	
    52	### Installation
    53	
    54	1. **Clone the repository**:
    55	   ```bash
    56	   git clone https://github.com/yourusername/diedrico.git
    57	   cd diedrico
    58	   ```
    59	
    60	2. **Install dependencies**:
    61	   ```bash
    62	   npm install
    63	   ```
    64	
    65	3. **Start the development server**:
    66	   ```bash
    67	   npm run dev
    68	   ```
    69	
    70	4. **Open in browser**:
    71	   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`
