   100	* [x] **Process Tree Expand Behavior (Phase 118)** - 📋 PLANNED
   101	  - **Problem**: Adding new elements expands all subprocesses in the process tree. Collapse state is stored in local `ref()` per component and is lost on re-render. No centralized state management for expand/collapse. Active subprocess is not tracked or visually indicated.
   102	  - **Solution**: Store collapse state in a Pinia store (keyed by node ID, persisted to localStorage). When new elements are added, only expand the receiving subprocess. Track and display the active subprocess distinctly.
