   105	
   106	## Phase 3: Render Fixed Elements
   107	
   108	**Purpose**: Display projection planes and coordinate system  
   109	**Reference**: [spec.md](./spec.md#projection-planes) - Projection Planes P_V and P_H, [spec.md](./spec.md#hinge-lines-hl-and-broken-hinge-lines-bhl) - Hinge Lines
   110	
   111	**Implementation Requirements**:
   112	- **Fixed Elements**: Must create per [spec.md §3D Elements](./spec.md#3d-elements-derived-not-edited): Origin point O at (0,0,0), planes P_V and P_H, hinge line HL_HV. These are ALWAYS present and cannot be deleted.
   113	- **Plane Definitions**: P_V (vertical, XZ plane at Y=0) and P_H (horizontal, XY plane at Z=0) per [spec.md §Coordinate System](./spec.md#coordinate-system-monge-projection). Must use point+normal representation from [data-model.md §Plane3DByPointAndNormal](./data-model.md#plane3dbypointandnormal).
   114	- **Coordinate Transformation**: Implement [data-model.md §Transformation Flow](./data-model.md#transformation-flow). Must support bidirectional transforms: plane intrinsic <u,v> ↔ canvas (x,y) for EACH plane.
   115	- **Three.js Matrices**: ALL transformations use Three.js `Matrix3` (3×3 for 2D). Non-destructive wrappers in threeUtils.ts: `applyMatrix3(vector, matrix)`, `invert(matrix)`.
   116	- **Visual Rendering**: Origin O = orange (#FF6B35), HL_HV = dashed gray (#333333) per [spec.md §Origin Point O](./spec.md#3d-elements-derived-not-edited).
   117	
   118	**⚠️ CRITICAL**: Study [data-model.md §Matrix Representations](./data-model.md#matrix-representations) to understand Three.js Matrix3 usage and custom Matrix4x3/Matrix3x4 for dimension changes.
   119	
