===== specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md =====
     1	# Feature Specification: Diedrico Dihedral Learning MVP
     2	
     3	**Feature Branch**: `001-dihedral-learning-mvp`  
     4	**Created**: 2025-12-22  
     5	**Status**: Draft  
     6	**Input**: Derived from `pre-spec.md` and `pre-spec-ui.md` (project documentation is in Spanish; this specification is intentionally in English per constitution).
     7	
     8	## Conceptual Model (User POV)
     9	
    10	This section defines the user-facing mental model, terminology, and UI components of the application. The goal is to make the *constructive process* explicit: the user performs deliberate operations, sees intermediate steps, and understands dependencies.
    11	
    12	### Purpose and Learning Focus
    13	
    14	- The application is an educational tool for **dihedral/orthographic projection** commonly taught in engineering programs.
    15	- The primary value is the **constructive process** (how the drawing is built), not only the final drawing.
    16	- The application does not “fix” mistakes or silently complete constructions; it surfaces infeasibility and lets the learner adjust inputs.
    17	
    18	### Workspace and Views
    19	
    20	From the user’s perspective, the workspace has two synchronized views:
    21	
    22	- **2D View (Primary)**: The main drawing area where all constructions are performed.
    23	  - The 2D view is where constructions are performed on the active plane; projection plane surfaces are visualized in the 3D overlay.
    24	  - One plane is always the **active plane** (new 2D elements are created there).
    25	  - Navigation is always available:
    26	    - Pan: `Shift` + drag
    27	    - Zoom: mouse wheel
    28	- **3D View (Auxiliary, Read-Only)**: A floating overlay used only to improve spatial understanding.
    29	  - Supports rotate, pan, zoom.
    30	  - Does not allow selecting or editing geometry.
    31	  - Can optionally show 2D elements on planes and linking visuals between 3D elements and their 2D projections.
    32	
    33	### Projection Planes
    34	
    35	A **projection plane** is a named 2D surface where the user draws 2D geometry.
    36	
    37	- Default planes:
    38	  - `P_H`: Horizontal plane (typically displayed horizontally in the 2D view)
    39	  - `P_V`: Vertical plane (typically displayed vertically in the 2D view)
    40	- **All projection planes are displayed simultaneously** in the 2D workspace, arranged in dihedral configuration around their shared hinge lines.
    41	- The system may include additional projection planes later (auxiliary, profile, etc.).
    42	- The **active plane** determines only *where new elements are created*; it does NOT control visibility.
    43	- Changing the active plane:
    44	  - does not hide or show planes,
    45	  - does not modify existing geometry,
    46	  - only changes which plane receives new constructions,
    47	  - updates visual emphasis (active plane elements at full intensity, others de-emphasized).
    48	
    49	### Hinge Lines (HL) and Broken Hinge Lines (BHL)
    50	
    51	A **hinge line** (HL) is the intersection line shared by two **projection planes** (the actual drawing planes themselves).
    52	
    53	- Naming convention: `HL_XY` where `X` and `Y` are plane identifiers.
    54	  - Example: `HL_HV` is the hinge line shared by `P_H` and `P_V` (the ground line).
    55	- Hinge lines are the **physical fold lines** between projection planes.
    56	- For geometric reasoning, hinge lines behave like regular 2D lines.
    57	
    58	**Architecture (Phase 84 - Canonical Coordinates)**:
    59	- **HingeLine** (3D entity): NO geometry storage. The 3D line is computed on-demand from canonical coordinates **(0,0,1)** (origin) and **(1,0,0)** (u-axis direction) in plane1's coordinate system, transformed to 3D via `HingeLine.realize3D()`.
    60	- **HalfHingeLine2D** (2D entity): Represents how the 3D hinge line appears in each plane's local coordinates. NO geometry storage - computed via `realize2D()`:
    61	  - **Plane1**: Returns canonical coordinates (0,0,1) and (1,0,0) directly
    62	  - **Plane2**: Projects the 3D line back to plane2 coordinates
    63	- **Key Insight**: Hinge line is ALWAYS at v=0 along the u-axis in plane intrinsic coordinates. This makes canonical coordinates universal for ALL hinge lines (base planes, auxiliary planes, etc.).
    64	
    65	**Benefits of Canonical Coordinates**:
    66	- Zero geometry duplication (was: stored in both HalfHingeLine2D objects)
    67	- Automatic parametric consistency (no validation needed)
    68	- Extensible to auxiliary projection planes with arbitrary orientations
    69	- Centralized 3D computation for rendering consistency
    70	
    71	**Broken Hinge Lines (BHL)**: When two arbitrary 3D planes intersect (not projection planes), their intersection line is called a **broken hinge line**. For example, with three planes A, B, C:
    72	- `HL_AB` and `HL_AC` are regular hinge lines (folds between projection planes)
    73	- `BHL_BC` is the broken hinge line (intersection of planes B and C in 3D space)
    74	- The BHL_BC appears as **projected lines** on planes B and C (two separate 2D Element lines)
    75	- Distance transport typically occurs between these BHL projections, not between regular HLs
    76	
    77	**Key difference**: Regular HLs are structural (fold lines). BHLs are geometric constructs whose projections are used for transport operations.
    78	
    79	### Guides
    80	
    81	A **guide** is a key dihedral learning construct:
    82	
    83	- Created from:
    84	  - a hinge line (HL or BHL projection), and
    85	  - a point on the active plane.
    86	- Result:
    87	  - a line **perpendicular** to the selected HL/BHL,
    88	  - belonging to **both** planes associated with that HL/BHL.
    89	
    90	**Important behavior with BHLs**: When a guide is created perpendicular to a BHL projection on one plane, it is **automatically transported** to the other plane's BHL projection. This establishes immediate geometric correspondence between the two projections.
    91	
    92	Guides enable transporting points and distances between planes in an explicit, traceable way.
    93	
    94	### 2D Elements (Explicit Entities)
    95	
    96	2D elements exist on exactly one projection plane and are created explicitly by the user:
    97	
    98	- Point
    99	- Segment
   100	- Line
   101	- Circle
   102	- Arc (optional)
   103	
   104	**No implicit entities rule (critical)**:
   105	- The UI must not create “implicit points” (e.g., a click somewhere along a segment is *not* treated as a point-on-segment).
   106	- If a later operation needs a point-on-curve/line/segment, the user must first create an explicit 2D point entity (e.g., point-on-element or intersection).
   107	
   108	#### Element Construction Methods
   109	
   110	Elements of the same type can be constructed in fundamentally different ways. Each construction method becomes a distinct **element variation** with its own creation tool and behavior:
   111	
   112	**Points**:
   113	- **Free Point**: User clicks to position anywhere on the active plane
   114	  - Tool: Free Point Tool
   115	  - Example: Drawing a triangle's vertices
   116	  - Special case: Origin points (O_H, O_V) are Free Points with locked=true
   117	
   118	**Note**: Intersection point variations (Line-Line, Line-Circle, Circle-Circle) will be added in future phases.
   119	
   120	**Lines**:
   121	- **Free Line**: User picks two existing points to define the line
   122	  - Tool: Line Tool + point selection
   123	  - Example: Connecting two traced points
   124	
   125	**Note**: Line variations (Parallel, Perpendicular) will be added in future phases.
   126	
   127	**Circles**:
   128	- **Circle by Center and Point**: Defined by center point and a point on the circumference
   129	  - Tool: Circle Tool + point selection
   130	  - Example: Creating an arc construction
   131	
   132	**Planes** (3D, created from 2D traces):
   133	- **Fixed Plane**: P_H and P_V with hard-coded orientations (**INITIALIZATION ONLY**)
   134	  - **CRITICAL**: NO user tool - users CANNOT create fixed planes via UI
   135	  - Created only during world initialization (bootstrapping)
   136	  - P_H at z=0 (horizontal), P_V at y=0 (vertical)
   137	  - This variation exists solely to represent the fundamental H and V projection planes
   138	
   139	**CRITICAL - Initialization-Only Elements**:
   140	- **Fixed Planes (Plane3DFixed)**: Created automatically during world setup, NO UI tools
   141	  - P_H and P_V only - these are the horizontal and vertical projection planes
   142	- **Origin points O_H, O_V**: Created as locked FreePoint2D during initialization
   143	- **Main hinge line HL_HV**: Created during world initialization
   144	
   145	**Note**: User-creatable plane variations (such as auxiliary planes) and 3D object manipulation are deferred to future phases when full 3D support is implemented.
   146	
   147	**Why Construction Methods Matter**:
   148	1. **Different parameters**: Free points need position; intersections need parent elements
   149	2. **Different dependencies**: Intersections update when parents move; free points don't
   150	3. **Different validity**: Intersections can become infeasible; free points can't
   151	4. **Different UI behavior**: Some need index selection; others don't
   152	5. **Different visualization**: Derived elements (intersections) appear de-emphasized
   153	
   154	The construction method is part of the element's identity and persists through undo/redo and save/load.
   155	### 3D Elements (Derived, Not Edited)
   156	
   157	3D elements are derived artifacts created explicitly from compatible 2D inputs:
   158	
   159	- 3D point: from two compatible 2D projections (e.g., a point projection on `P_H` and a point projection on `P_V`).
   160	- 3D line: from compatible 2D projections.
   161	- 3D segment: from two compatible 2D segments (one per plane) with compatible endpoints.
   162	- 3D plane: from compatible 2D traces.
   163	
   164	3D elements:
   165	- are not edited directly,
   166	- exist as a consequence of 2D constructions,
   167	- are visualized in the 3D view to support learning.
   168	
   169	**Origin Point O** (special 3D element):
   170	
   171	Every workspace contains a special **origin point** named `O`:
   172	
   173	- `O` is a **3D element** defined by hardcoded coordinates (0, 0, 0) in 3D space.
   174	- Type: `Point3DByCoordinates` (not derived from projections)
   175	- Geometrically, it sits at the intersection of projection planes `P_H` and `P_V` (on the hinge line `HL_HV`).
   176	- Its 2D projections are **stored as 2D Point objects** in the World:
   177	  - `O_H` on `P_H`: locked Point with local coordinates (0, 0) — on the hinge line
   178	  - `O_V` on `P_V`: locked Point with local coordinates (0, 0) — on the hinge line
   179	- The 3D point `O` is **defined by** its two projections `O_H` and `O_V` (standard dihedral geometry).
   180	- The origin point is **always present** from the moment a workspace is created.
   181	- It is always visible and cannot be deleted or moved (points are locked).
   182	- It can be used as a reference point in constructions like any other 3D point.
   183	- Visual appearance: regular point rendering (not a special crosshair), distinguishable by color (#FF6B35 orange).
   184	
   185	**Projection Planes P_H and P_V** (special 3D elements):
   186	
   187	Every workspace contains two fundamental **projection planes** defined by point + normal vector:
   188	
   189	- `P_H`: Horizontal projection plane
   190	  - Type: `Plane3DByPointAndNormal`
   191	  - Origin: point `O` (0, 0, 0)
   192	  - Normal vector: (0, 0, 1) — pointing upward along Z-axis
   193	  - The plane where "top views" are drawn
   194	- `P_V`: Vertical projection plane
   195	  - Type: `Plane3DByPointAndNormal`
   196	  - Origin: point `O` (0, 0, 0)
   197	  - Normal vector: (0, 1, 0) — pointing toward viewer along Y-axis
   198	  - The plane where "front views" are drawn
   199	
   200	These planes are **always present**, cannot be deleted, and serve as the fundamental reference surfaces for dihedral projection.
   201	
   202	**Hinge Line HL_HV** (special 3D element):
   203	
   204	The hinge line between `P_H` and `P_V`:
   205	
   206	- `HL_HV` is a **3D element** defined as the intersection of two planes.
   207	- Type: `Line3DFromPlaneIntersection`
   208	- Defined by: intersection of `P_H` and `P_V`
   209	- 3D position: X-axis where y=0 AND z=0 (parametric: (x, 0, 0) for all x)
   210	- Its 2D projections (`HL_HV_H`, `HL_HV_V`) appear as horizontal lines on each plane:
   211	  - `HL_HV_H` on `P_H`: horizontal line at v = 0 (plane intrinsic coordinates)
   212	  - `HL_HV_V` on `P_V`: horizontal line at v = 0 (plane intrinsic coordinates)
   213	- Visual appearance: dashed gray line (#333333)
   214	- The hinge line is the "fold line" or "ground line" in traditional dihedral drawings
   215	- Position is derived from plane intersection, not hardcoded (v=0 is the geometric result)
   216	- It is **always present** and cannot be deleted
   217	
   218	### Coordinate System (Monge Projection)
   219	
   220	The application uses **Monge projection** (descriptive geometry) with the following coordinate system conventions:

===== frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue =====
     1	<template>
     2	  <div class="svg-canvas-container">
     3	    <svg
     4	      ref="svgElement"
     5	      class="svg-canvas"
     6	      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
     7	      :viewBox="`0 0 ${canvasWidth} ${canvasHeight}`"
     8	      preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
     9	      @mousedown="handleMouseDown"
    10	      @click="handleCanvasClick"
    11	      @dblclick="handleDoubleClick"
    12	      @mousemove="handleMouseMove"
    13	      @wheel.prevent="handleWheel"
    14	    >
    15	      <!-- Background grid (T275) - Zoom-adaptive grid display -->
    16	      <g v-if="viewStore.gridVisible.value" class="background-grid">
    17	        <line
    18	          v-for="line in gridLines"
    19	          :key="line.key"
    20	          :x1="line.x1"
    21	          :y1="line.y1"
    22	          :x2="line.x2"
    23	          :y2="line.y2"
    24	          :stroke="line.major ? '#C0C0C0' : '#E0E0E0'"
    25	          :stroke-width="line.major ? 1 : 0.5"
    26	        />
    27	      </g>
    28	      
    29	      <!-- Render all lines through canvas presentation model (including HL_HV projections) -->
    30	      <line
    31	        v-for="{ primitive, attrs } in renderedLines"
    32	        :key="primitive.id"
    33	        v-bind="attrs"
    34	      />
    35	      
    36	      <!-- Render all segments through canvas presentation model -->
    37	      <line
    38	        v-for="{ primitive, attrs } in renderedSegments"
    39	        :key="primitive.id"
    40	        v-bind="attrs"
    41	      />
    42	      
    43	      <!-- Render all guides through canvas presentation model -->
    44	      <line
    45	        v-for="{ primitive, attrs } in renderedGuides"
    46	        :key="primitive.id"
    47	        v-bind="attrs"
    48	      />
    49	      
    50	      <!-- Render all circles through canvas presentation model -->
    51	      <circle
    52	        v-for="{ primitive, attrs } in renderedCircles"
    53	        :key="primitive.id"
    54	        v-bind="attrs"
    55	      />
    56	      
    57	      <!-- Render all arcs through canvas presentation model -->
    58	      <path
    59	        v-for="{ primitive, attrs } in renderedArcs"
    60	        :key="primitive.id"
    61	        v-bind="attrs"
    62	      />
    63	      
    64	      <!-- Render all points through canvas presentation model -->
    65	      <circle
    66	        v-for="{ primitive, attrs } in renderedPoints"
    67	        :key="primitive.id"
    68	        v-bind="attrs"
    69	      />
    70	      
    71	      <!-- Snap preview indicator - orange glow around snap target point -->
    72	      <circle
    73	        v-if="snapTarget.pointId && snapTarget.position"
    74	        :cx="snapTarget.position.x"
    75	        :cy="snapTarget.position.y"
    76	        :r="8"
    77	        fill="none"
    78	        stroke="#FF6B35"
    79	        stroke-width="2"
    80	        opacity="0.8"
    81	        class="snap-indicator"
    82	      />
    83	      
    84	      <!-- Grid coordinate labels (Phase 78) - Display u,v values at viewport borders -->
    85	      <g v-if="viewStore.gridVisible.value" class="grid-labels">
    86	        <!-- Top edge labels (U-coordinates) -->
    87	        <text
    88	          v-for="label in gridLabels.top"
    89	          :key="label.key"
    90	          :x="label.position"
    91	          :y="12"
    92	          class="grid-label"
    93	          text-anchor="middle"
    94	        >
    95	          {{ label.value }}
    96	        </text>
    97	        
    98	        <!-- Bottom edge labels (U-coordinates) -->
    99	        <text
   100	          v-for="label in gridLabels.bottom"
   101	          :key="label.key"
   102	          :x="label.position"
   103	          :y="canvasHeight - 4"
   104	          class="grid-label"
   105	          text-anchor="middle"
   106	        >
   107	          {{ label.value }}
   108	        </text>
   109	        
   110	        <!-- Left edge labels (V-coordinates) -->
   111	        <text
   112	          v-for="label in gridLabels.left"
   113	          :key="label.key"
   114	          :x="4"
   115	          :y="label.position"
   116	          class="grid-label"
   117	          text-anchor="start"
   118	          dominant-baseline="middle"
   119	        >
   120	          {{ label.value }}
   121	        </text>
   122	        
   123	        <!-- Right edge labels (V-coordinates) -->
   124	        <text
   125	          v-for="label in gridLabels.right"
   126	          :key="label.key"
   127	          :x="canvasWidth - 4"
   128	          :y="label.position"
   129	          class="grid-label"
   130	          text-anchor="end"
   131	          dominant-baseline="middle"
   132	        >
   133	          {{ label.value }}
   134	        </text>
   135	      </g>
   136	    </svg>
   137	    
   138	    <!-- Hover tooltip -->
   139	    <div 
   140	      v-if="hoverHighlight.isHovering.value && hoverHighlight.hoveredElementLabel.value && hoverHighlight.temporary && !hoverHighlight.temporary.value"
   141	      class="hover-tooltip"
   142	      :style="{ left: tooltipPosition.x + 'px', top: tooltipPosition.y + 'px' }"
   143	    >
   144	      {{ hoverHighlight.hoveredElementLabel.value }}
   145	    </div>
   146	    
   147	    <!-- Properties Dialog -->
   148	    <PropertiesDialog
   149	      :is-open="showPropertiesDialog"
   150	      :element-id="propertiesElementId"
   151	      :world="world"
   152	      @close="showPropertiesDialog = false"
   153	      @save="handleSaveProperties"
   154	    />
   155	  </div>
   156	</template>
   157	
   158	<script setup lang="ts">
   159	/**
   160	 * SvgCanvas.vue - Main 2D drawing canvas component
   161	 * 
   162	 * This is the primary workspace where all 2D geometric elements are rendered.
   163	 * Uses SVG for crisp, scalable vector graphics per Constitution Principle IV.
   164	 * 
   165	 * Rendering Pipeline:
   166	 * 1. World (domain objects + realizations) 
   167	 * 2. → CanvasPresentationSelector (generates read-model primitives in paper coordinates)
   168	 * 3. → SVGRenderer (applies viewport transform, generates SVG attributes)
   169	 * 4. → SVG elements
   170	 * 
   171	 * Key requirements:
   172	 * - SVG element (not HTML Canvas) per ui-spec.md
   173	 * - Rendering consumes the canvas presentation read model
   174	 * - Generic rendering algorithms (no special cases for fixed elements)
   175	 * - Will support pan/zoom viewport transformations in Phase 6
   176	 * - Elements rendered using principle-based algorithms (Constitution Principle IV)
   177	 * 
   178	 * @see specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/ui-spec.md#canvas-component
   179	 */
   180	
   181	import { ref, computed, watch, onMounted, onUnmounted, inject, provide } from 'vue';
   182	import { Matrix3, Vector3 } from 'three';
   183	import { World } from '@/domain/world/World';
   184	import { SVGRenderer, type ViewportTransform } from '@/services/SVGRenderer';
   185	import { InputService } from '@/services/InputService';
   186	import { PointTool } from '@/tools/PointTool';
   187	import { LineTool } from '@/tools/LineTool';
   188	import { SegmentTool } from '@/tools/SegmentTool';
   189	import { CircleTool } from '@/tools/CircleTool';
   190	import { GuideTool } from '@/tools/GuideTool';
   191	import { IntersectionTool } from '@/tools/IntersectionTool';
   192	import { ParallelLineTool } from '@/tools/ParallelLineTool';
   193	import { PerpendicularLineTool } from '@/tools/PerpendicularLineTool';
   194	import { TangentLineToCircleThroughPointTool } from '@/tools/TangentLineToCircleThroughPointTool';
   195	import { TangentLineToCircleParallelToLineTool } from '@/tools/TangentLineToCircleParallelToLineTool';
   196	import { Create3DPointTool } from '@/tools/Create3DPointTool';
   197	import { Create3DLineTool } from '@/tools/Create3DLineTool';
   198	import { Create3DSegmentTool } from '@/tools/Create3DSegmentTool';
   199	import { Create3DPlaneTool } from '@/tools/Create3DPlaneTool';
   200	import { CreateProjectionPlaneTool } from '@/tools/CreateProjectionPlaneTool';
   201	import { FreePoint2D } from '@/domain/world/Point';
   202	import { useToolStore } from '@/stores/toolStore';
   203	import { useViewStore } from '@/stores/viewStore';
   204	import { useSelectionStore } from '@/stores/selectionStore';
   205	import { useViewport } from '@/composables/useViewport';
   206	import { useGlobalHoverHighlight } from '@/composables/useHoverHighlight';
   207	import { screenTo3D } from '@/utils/coordinateTransform';
   208	import PropertiesDialog from '@/components/dialogs/PropertiesDialog.vue';
   209	import type { ITool } from '@/tools/ITool';
   210	import { createCanvasToolController } from '@/application/tools/CanvasToolController';
   211	import type { FreePointMoveSession } from '@/application/tools/ToolCommandIntents';
   212	import { CanvasPresentationController } from '@/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasPresentationController';
   213	import { CanvasInteractionQuery } from '@/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasInteractionQuery';
   214	
   215	// Define emits
   216	const emit = defineEmits<{
   217	  'update-3d-coordinates': [coords: { x: number; y: number; z: number } | null];
   218	  'update-active-plane': [planeInfo: { id: string; name: string }];
   219	}>();
   220	

===== frontend/src/stores/toolStore.ts =====
     1	/**
     2	 * toolStore.ts - Tool selection state management
     3	 * 
     4	 * Manages the currently active geometric construction tool.
     5	 * When a tool is selected, the canvas changes its interaction mode
     6	 * to match the tool's behavior (point placement, line creation, etc.)
     7	 * 
     8	 * Supports tool families with dropdown menus, last-used sub-tool memory,
     9	 * and configurable completion behavior (stay-active vs return-to-selection).
    10	 * 
    11	 * Reference: specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/ui-spec.md - Tool Interactions
    12	 * Reference: specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/data-model.md - Phase 67
    13	 */
    14	
    15	import { ref, computed } from 'vue';
    16	import type { ToolFamilyConfig, ToolConfig } from '../types/ToolConfig';
    17	
    18	export const TOOL_TYPE = {
    19	  SELECT: 'select',
    20	  POINT: 'point',
    21	  LINE: 'line',
    22	  CIRCLE: 'circle',
    23	  SEGMENT: 'segment',
    24	  GUIDE: 'guide',
    25	  INTERSECTION: 'intersection',
    26	  TRANSPORT: 'transport',
    27	  PARALLEL_LINE: 'parallel-line',
    28	  PERPENDICULAR_LINE: 'perpendicular-line',
    29	  TANGENT_LINE_TO_CIRCLE_THROUGH_POINT: 'tangent-line-to-circle-through-point',
    30	  TANGENT_LINE_TO_CIRCLE_PARALLEL: 'tangent-line-to-circle-parallel',
    31	  CREATE3DPOINT: 'create3dpoint',
    32	  CREATE3DLINE: 'create3dline',
    33	  CREATE3DSEGMENT: 'create3dsegment',
    34	  CREATE3DPLANE: 'create3dplane',
    35	  CREATEPROJECTIONPLANE: 'createprojectionplane',
    36	  INTERACTIVEPROJECTIONSETUP: 'interactiveprojectionsetup',
    37	  QUICKPROJECTIONSETUP: 'quickprojectionsetup',
    38	  QUICK3DLINE: 'quick3dline',
    39	  QUICK3DSEGMENT: 'quick3dsegment',
    40	} as const;
    41	export type ToolType = typeof TOOL_TYPE[keyof typeof TOOL_TYPE];
    42	
    43	const STORAGE_KEY = 'diedrico-tool-last-used';
    44	
    45	const activeTool = ref<ToolType>('select');
    46	const lastUsedByFamily = ref<Record<string, string>>({});
    47	const toolStepMessage = ref<string>('');
    48	let toolFamilies: ToolFamilyConfig[] = [];
    49	
    50	// Load last-used preferences from localStorage on module initialization
    51	function loadFromLocalStorage(): Record<string, string> {
    52	  try {
    53	    const stored = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
    54	    return stored ? JSON.parse(stored) : {};
    55	  } catch (error) {
    56	    console.warn('Failed to load last-used tool preferences:', error);
    57	    return {};
    58	  }
    59	}
    60	
    61	// Save last-used preferences to localStorage
    62	function saveToLocalStorage(lastUsed: Record<string, string>): void {
    63	  try {
    64	    localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(lastUsed));
    65	  } catch (error) {
    66	    console.warn('Failed to save last-used tool preferences:', error);
    67	  }
    68	}
    69	
    70	// Initialize lastUsedByFamily from localStorage
    71	lastUsedByFamily.value = loadFromLocalStorage();
    72	
    73	export function useToolStore() {
    74	  /**
    75	   * Set the active tool
    76	   */
    77	  function setTool(tool: ToolType) {
    78	    activeTool.value = tool;
    79	    toolStepMessage.value = ''; // Clear step message when tool changes
    80	  }
    81	
    82	  /**
    83	   * Check if a specific tool is active
    84	   */
    85	  function isToolActive(tool: ToolType): boolean {
    86	    return activeTool.value === tool;
    87	  }
    88	
    89	  /**
    90	   * Get the current active tool
    91	   */
    92	  const currentTool = computed(() => activeTool.value);
    93	
    94	  /**
    95	   * Initialize tool families configuration
    96	   * Must be called once with TOOL_FAMILIES from config
    97	   */
    98	  function setToolFamilies(families: ToolFamilyConfig[]) {
    99	    toolFamilies = families;
   100	  }
   101	
   102	  /**
   103	   * Find the family that contains the given tool
   104	   */
   105	  function getToolFamily(toolId: string): ToolFamilyConfig | undefined {
   106	    return toolFamilies.find(family => 
   107	      family.tools.some(tool => tool.id === toolId)
   108	    );
   109	  }
   110	
   111	  /**
   112	   * Get configuration for a specific tool
   113	   */
   114	  function getToolConfig(toolId: string): ToolConfig | undefined {
   115	    for (const family of toolFamilies) {
   116	      const tool = family.tools.find(t => t.id === toolId);
   117	      if (tool) return tool;
   118	    }
   119	    return undefined;
   120	  }
   121	
   122	  /**
   123	   * Get completion behavior for a tool
   124	   */
   125	  function getCompletionBehavior(toolId: string): 'stay-active' | 'return-to-selection' | undefined {
   126	    const config = getToolConfig(toolId);
   127	    return config?.completionBehavior;
   128	  }
   129	
   130	  /**
   131	   * Activate a tool family - uses last-used sub-tool or default
   132	   */
   133	  function activateToolFamily(familyId: string): void {
   134	    const family = toolFamilies.find(f => f.id === familyId);
   135	    if (!family) {
   136	      console.warn(`Tool family not found: ${familyId}`);
   137	      return;
   138	    }
   139	
   140	    // Use last-used tool for this family, or default if none
   141	    const toolId = lastUsedByFamily.value[familyId] || family.defaultTool;
   142	    setTool(toolId as ToolType);
   143	  }
   144	
   145	  /**
   146	   * Select a specific sub-tool and update last-used memory
   147	   */
   148	  function selectSubTool(familyId: string, toolId: string): void {
   149	    // Update last-used for this family
   150	    lastUsedByFamily.value[familyId] = toolId;
   151	    saveToLocalStorage(lastUsedByFamily.value);
   152	    
   153	    // Activate the tool
   154	    setTool(toolId as ToolType);
   155	  }
   156	
   157	  /**
   158	   * Get the last-used tool for a family (for UI state)
   159	   */
   160	  function getLastUsedTool(familyId: string): string | undefined {
   161	    return lastUsedByFamily.value[familyId];
   162	  }
   163	
   164	  /**
   165	   * Phase 115: Set contextual tool step feedback message
   166	   */
   167	  function setToolStepMessage(message: string) {
   168	    toolStepMessage.value = message;
   169	  }
   170	
   171	  /**
   172	   * Phase 115: Get reactive tool step message
   173	   */
   174	  const currentToolStepMessage = computed(() => toolStepMessage.value);
   175	
   176	  return {
   177	    currentTool,
   178	    currentToolStepMessage,
   179	    setTool,
   180	    setToolStepMessage,
   181	    isToolActive,
   182	    setToolFamilies,
   183	    getToolFamily,
   184	    getToolConfig,
   185	    getCompletionBehavior,
   186	    activateToolFamily,
   187	    selectSubTool,
   188	    getLastUsedTool
   189	  };
   190	}

===== frontend/src/stores/settingsStore.ts =====
     1	/**
     2	 * Settings Store - User preferences and application settings
     3	 * 
     4	 * Manages user-configurable settings with localStorage persistence.
     5	 * Settings are loaded on application startup and saved automatically on change.
     6	 * 
     7	 * Settings Categories:
     8	 * - Grid: Visibility, spacing, style, snap-to-grid
     9	 * - Snap: Enable/disable, snap radius (in pixels)
    10	 * - Default Styles: Colors, line widths for new elements
    11	 * - 3D View: Initial camera position, display options
    12	 * 
    13	 * @see specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/ui-spec.md#project-settings-dialog
    14	 * @see specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/ui-spec.md#state-persistence
    15	 */
    16	
    17	import { ref, computed, watch } from 'vue';
    18	import { defineStore } from 'pinia';
    19	
    20	const STORAGE_KEY = 'diedrico_settings_v1';
    21	
    22	/**
    23	 * Default settings values
    24	 * Following ui-spec.md recommendations
    25	 */
    26	const DEFAULT_SETTINGS = {
    27	  // Grid settings
    28	  grid: {
    29	    visible: true,
    30	    spacing: 20, // Base spacing in world units (adapts with zoom)
    31	    color: '#E0E0E0',
    32	    snapToGrid: false,
    33	  },
    34	  
    35	  // Snap settings
    36	  snap: {
    37	    enabled: true,
    38	    radius: 12, // Snap radius in screen pixels (10-15 per spec)
    39	  },
    40	  
    41	  // Default visual styles for new elements
    42	  defaultStyles: {
    43	    pointColor: '#000000',
    44	    pointSize: 3, // Radius in pixels
    45	    lineColor: '#000000',
    46	    lineWidth: 1.5, // In pixels
    47	    circleColor: '#000000',
    48	    circleWidth: 1.5,
    49	    guideColor: '#666666',
    50	    guideWidth: 1,
    51	    guideDashed: true,
    52	  },
    53	  
    54	  // 3D view settings
    55	  view3D: {
    56	    showPlanes: true,
    57	    showProjectionLines: true,
    58	    show2DElements: true,
    59	    initialCameraDistance: 10,
    60	  },
    61	};
    62	
    63	export interface Settings {
    64	  grid: {
    65	    visible: boolean;
    66	    spacing: number;
    67	    color: string;
    68	    snapToGrid: boolean;
    69	  };
    70	  snap: {
    71	    enabled: boolean;
    72	    radius: number;
    73	  };
    74	  defaultStyles: {
    75	    pointColor: string;
    76	    pointSize: number;
    77	    lineColor: string;
    78	    lineWidth: number;
    79	    circleColor: string;
    80	    circleWidth: number;
    81	    guideColor: string;
    82	    guideWidth: number;
    83	    guideDashed: boolean;
    84	  };
    85	  view3D: {
    86	    showPlanes: boolean;
    87	    showProjectionLines: boolean;
    88	    show2DElements: boolean;
    89	    initialCameraDistance: number;
    90	  };
    91	}
    92	
    93	export const useSettingsStore = defineStore('settings', () => {
    94	  // Settings state (initialized from localStorage or defaults)
    95	  const settings = ref<Settings>(loadSettings());
    96	  
    97	  /**
    98	   * Load settings from localStorage
    99	   * Falls back to defaults if not found or invalid
   100	   */
   101	  function loadSettings(): Settings {
   102	    try {
   103	      const stored = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
   104	      if (stored) {
   105	        const parsed = JSON.parse(stored);
   106	        // Merge with defaults to handle new settings in updates
   107	        return {
   108	          grid: { ...DEFAULT_SETTINGS.grid, ...(parsed.grid || {}) },
   109	          snap: { ...DEFAULT_SETTINGS.snap, ...(parsed.snap || {}) },
   110	          defaultStyles: { ...DEFAULT_SETTINGS.defaultStyles, ...(parsed.defaultStyles || {}) },
   111	          view3D: { ...DEFAULT_SETTINGS.view3D, ...(parsed.view3D || {}) },
   112	        };
   113	      }
   114	    } catch (error) {
   115	      console.warn('[SettingsStore] Failed to load settings from localStorage:', error);
   116	    }
   117	    return structuredClone(DEFAULT_SETTINGS);
   118	  }
   119	  
   120	  /**
   121	   * Save settings to localStorage
   122	   */
   123	  function saveSettings() {
   124	    try {
   125	      localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(settings.value));
   126	      console.log('[SettingsStore] Settings saved to localStorage');
   127	    } catch (error) {
   128	      console.error('[SettingsStore] Failed to save settings to localStorage:', error);
   129	    }
   130	  }
   131	  
   132	  /**
   133	   * Watch for settings changes and auto-save
   134	   */
   135	  watch(settings, () => {
   136	    saveSettings();
   137	  }, { deep: true });
   138	  
   139	  // Grid settings
   140	  const gridVisible = computed({
   141	    get: () => settings.value.grid.visible,
   142	    set: (value: boolean) => {
   143	      settings.value.grid.visible = value;
   144	    },
   145	  });
   146	  
   147	  const gridSpacing = computed({
   148	    get: () => settings.value.grid.spacing,
   149	    set: (value: number) => {
   150	      settings.value.grid.spacing = value;
   151	    },
   152	  });
   153	  
   154	  const gridColor = computed({
   155	    get: () => settings.value.grid.color,
   156	    set: (value: string) => {
   157	      settings.value.grid.color = value;
   158	    },
   159	  });
   160	  
   161	  const snapToGrid = computed({
   162	    get: () => settings.value.grid.snapToGrid,
   163	    set: (value: boolean) => {
   164	      settings.value.grid.snapToGrid = value;
   165	    },
   166	  });
   167	  
   168	  // Snap settings
   169	  const snapEnabled = computed({
   170	    get: () => settings.value.snap.enabled,
   171	    set: (value: boolean) => {
   172	      settings.value.snap.enabled = value;
   173	    },
   174	  });
   175	  
   176	  const snapRadius = computed({
   177	    get: () => settings.value.snap.radius,
   178	    set: (value: number) => {
   179	      settings.value.snap.radius = value;
   180	    },
   181	  });
   182	  
   183	  // Default style getters (read-only for now)
   184	  const defaultPointColor = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.pointColor);
   185	  const defaultPointSize = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.pointSize);
   186	  const defaultLineColor = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.lineColor);
   187	  const defaultLineWidth = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.lineWidth);
   188	  const defaultCircleColor = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.circleColor);
   189	  const defaultCircleWidth = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.circleWidth);
   190	  const defaultGuideColor = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.guideColor);
   191	  const defaultGuideWidth = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.guideWidth);
   192	  const defaultGuideDashed = computed(() => settings.value.defaultStyles.guideDashed);
   193	  
   194	  // 3D view settings getters (read-only for now)
   195	  const showPlanes = computed(() => settings.value.view3D.showPlanes);
   196	  const showProjectionLines = computed(() => settings.value.view3D.showProjectionLines);
   197	  const show2DElements = computed(() => settings.value.view3D.show2DElements);
   198	  const initialCameraDistance = computed(() => settings.value.view3D.initialCameraDistance);
   199	  
   200	  /**
   201	   * Update a specific setting
   202	   */
   203	  function updateSetting(path: string, value: any) {
   204	    const keys = path.split('.');
   205	    let target: any = settings.value;
   206	    
   207	    for (let i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) {
   208	      target = target[keys[i]];
   209	    }
   210	    
   211	    target[keys[keys.length - 1]] = value;
   212	  }
   213	  
   214	  /**
   215	   * Reset all settings to defaults
   216	   */
   217	  function resetToDefaults() {
   218	    settings.value = structuredClone(DEFAULT_SETTINGS);
   219	    console.log('[SettingsStore] Settings reset to defaults');
   220	  }

